proof.text:
For $M$ a module sheaf on $X_{\mathrm{proet}}$, the comparison definition states $(
u_{X*}M)(W	o X)=M(W	o X)$ for etale $W	o X$, and the same formula on arrows. Consequently for every etale $W	o U$ the restrictions of steps 1 and 2 give
$$ (r_j^{\mathrm{et}}
u_{X*}M)(W	o U)=M(W	o X)=(
u_{U*}r_j^{\mathrm{pro}}M)(W	o U). $$
Both maps along $W'	o W$ are the restriction map of $M$ along that same scheme morphism; both scalar operations are those of $M$. The identity on these sections therefore defines a module-sheaf natural isomorphism $	heta_{j,M}:r_j^{\mathrm{et}}
u_{X*}M\xrightarrow{\sim}
u_{U*}r_j^{\mathrm{pro}}M$. It is natural in $M$ since both sides send a map $M	o N$ to its component at $W	o X$. For $V\xrightarrow{k}U\xrightarrow{j}X$, both the direct identification $	heta_{jk}$ and the pasted identifications $	heta_j,	heta_k$ are the identity of $M(W	o V	o U	o X)$; for $j=\mathrm{id}$ the identification is the identity as well.
